 ("Somatostatin reduces acid secretion by binding a receptor coupled to:",["Gi, inhibiting adenylyl cyclase","Gs, stimulating adenylyl cyclase","Gq, stimulating phospholipase C","A tyrosine kinase domain"],0,"Somatostatin and prostaglandins act through Gi on the parietal cell."),
 ("The 'alkaline tide' after a meal results from:",["Basolateral HCO₃⁻ exit from parietal cells","Pancreatic HCO₃⁻ absorbed in the jejunum","Brunner gland HCO₃⁻ entering the blood","Renal HCO₃⁻ reabsorption after vomiting"],0,"For each H⁺ secreted, HCO₃⁻ leaves basolaterally via Cl⁻/HCO₃⁻ exchange, raising gastric venous pH."),
